IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-interpretation`
IMPORT `g6-art18-governor-duties`
IMPORT `g6-art20-court-orders`
IMPORT `g6-art19-reportable-matters`

-- g6-tests-art19.l4: tests of Article 19 (Reportable matters and acting as a governor).
-- Every expected value was decided from the text of the Law before the module was first run; the quotation above a group is the text it comes from.
-- A DEONTIC cannot be compared in #ASSERT, so duties, powers and prohibitions are exercised by #TRACE, each with its outcome in the `-- EXPECT:` comment above it
-- (read by work/g6/check-traces.py); the facts behind them are asserted on the BOOLEAN rules. Dates: a trace on a date-serial clock starts AT (Day (YMD ...)).

§ `Tests of Article 19`

§§ `Fixtures`

`Gwen with no reportable matter` MEANS Governor WITH
    name IS "Gwen"
    `is a natural person` IS TRUE
    `is resident in Jersey` IS TRUE
    `is itself a Jersey entity by virtue of Article 2(3)(a)` IS FALSE
    `reportable matters` IS EMPTY

`Gus with a reportable matter` MEANS Governor WITH
    name IS "Gus"
    `is a natural person` IS TRUE
    `is resident in Jersey` IS TRUE
    `is itself a Jersey entity by virtue of Article 2(3)(a)` IS FALSE
    `reportable matters` IS LIST `bankruptcy or other insolvency`

`an entity applying for registration` MEANS Entity WITH
    name IS "Applicant Trust"
    `standing on the register` IS `an applicant for registration`
    `kinds of entity` IS LIST `the trustees of a trust`
    `is a Jersey entity` IS TRUE
    governors IS LIST `Gwen with no reportable matter`
    purposes IS EMPTY

`a registered charity entity` MEANS Entity WITH
    name IS "Hope Society"
    `standing on the register` IS `entered in the general section`
    `kinds of entity` IS LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`
    `is a Jersey entity` IS TRUE
    governors IS LIST `Gwen with no reportable matter`
    purposes IS EMPTY

`an entity not on the register` MEANS Entity WITH
    name IS "Nobody Ltd"
    `standing on the register` IS `not on the register`
    `kinds of entity` IS LIST `a company`
    `is a Jersey entity` IS TRUE
    governors IS LIST `Gwen with no reportable matter`
    purposes IS EMPTY

`the register entry of an ordinary charity` MEANS `Registered charity` WITH
    entity IS `a registered charity entity`
    `registration number` IS "1"
    `registered name` IS "Hope Society"
    `alternative registered names` IS EMPTY
    `date registered` IS YMD 2019 1 1
    `date deregistered` IS NOTHING
    `registered charitable purposes` IS LIST "relief of poverty"
    `registered public benefit statement` IS "relief"
    `is an organized religious charity` IS FALSE

`the register entry of an organized religious charity` MEANS `Registered charity` WITH
    entity IS `a registered charity entity`
    `registration number` IS "2"
    `registered name` IS "Faith Society"
    `alternative registered names` IS EMPTY
    `date registered` IS YMD 2019 1 1
    `date deregistered` IS NOTHING
    `registered charitable purposes` IS LIST "advancement of religion"
    `registered public benefit statement` IS "worship"
    `is an organized religious charity` IS TRUE

`a required steps notice served on the charity` MEANS `Required steps notice` WITH
    `served on` IS `the registered charity`
    `prompted by` IS `there has been misconduct by a registered charity`
    `date served` IS YMD 2026 1 15
    `steps to be taken by` IS NOTHING
    `requires a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced` IS FALSE
    `has been complied with` IS FALSE

`the notices served` MEANS LIST `a required steps notice served on the charity`

§§ `Article 19(1) -- the eight reportable matters`

-- Positional construction of the facts about a person; the columns, in the order of the record: conduct as a governor; the governors of the charity; the conduct of the charity is misconduct
-- within Article 2(10); the misconduct led to a required steps notice; disqualification orders under this Law; another restriction under this Law; disqualifications as a charity trustee
-- or an equivalent; disqualifications as a company director or an equivalent outside Jersey; bankrupt or otherwise insolvent; convictions; falls within a description prescribed by Order.
--
`Ann clean` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Ann", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`Abe concurs` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Abe", FALSE, TRUE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`Bea assists Abe` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Bea", FALSE, FALSE, (LIST "Abe"), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`Cal assists Bea` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Cal", FALSE, FALSE, (LIST "Bea"), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`the board of Abe, Bea and Cal` MEANS LIST `Abe concurs`, `Bea assists Abe`, `Cal assists Bea`

`Ann has nothing reportable` MEANS `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` OF `Ann clean`, (LIST `Ann clean`), FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE
`Abe whose misconduct led to a notice` MEANS `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` OF `Abe concurs`, `the board of Abe, Bea and Cal`, TRUE, TRUE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE
`Abe whose misconduct led to no notice` MEANS `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` OF `Abe concurs`, `the board of Abe, Bea and Cal`, TRUE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE
`Cal whose misconduct is by assisting and led to a notice` MEANS `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` OF `Cal assists Bea`, `the board of Abe, Bea and Cal`, TRUE, TRUE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE
`Ann clean but a notice is said to have been led to` MEANS `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` OF `Ann clean`, (LIST `Ann clean`), FALSE, TRUE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE

-- src:484 | (a) has engaged in misconduct as a governor of a registered charity, being misconduct that led to the service of a required steps notice on that governor or on that charity or on another governor of that charity;
-- (a) has engaged in misconduct as a governor ... that led to the service of a required steps notice. Misconduct under Article 18(4) AND the link to a notice AND a notice served.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1)(a) the person has engaged in misconduct as a governor that led to a required steps notice` `the readings taken` `the notices served` `Abe whose misconduct led to a notice`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(1)(a) the person has engaged in misconduct as a governor that led to a required steps notice` `the readings taken` `the notices served` `Abe whose misconduct led to no notice`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(1)(a) the person has engaged in misconduct as a governor that led to a required steps notice` `the readings taken` `the notices served` `Ann clean but a notice is said to have been led to`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(1)(a) the person has engaged in misconduct as a governor that led to a required steps notice` `the readings taken` EMPTY `Abe whose misconduct led to a notice`
-- Misconduct reached by assisting (Article 18(4)(c)) is misconduct as a governor for the purpose of (a).
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1)(a) the person has engaged in misconduct as a governor that led to a required steps notice` `the readings taken` `the notices served` `Cal whose misconduct is by assisting and led to a notice`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(1)(a) the person has engaged in misconduct as a governor that led to a required steps notice` `the readings taken` `the notices served` `Ann has nothing reportable`

-- Orders and persons for (b).
`an order against Orla from 1 January 2025 to 31 December 2030` MEANS `Disqualification order` OF "Orla", YMD 2025 1 1, YMD 2030 12 31
`Orla subject to an order` MEANS `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` OF (`Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Orla", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, (LIST `an order against Orla from 1 January 2025 to 31 December 2030`), FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE
`Orla subject to an order made against somebody else` MEANS `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` OF (`Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Orla", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, (LIST (`Disqualification order` OF "Ivor", YMD 2025 1 1, YMD 2030 12 31)), FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE
`Rex subject to another restriction under this Law` MEANS `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` OF (`Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Rex", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, TRUE, EMPTY, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE

-- src:485 | (b) is the subject of a disqualification order, or of any other restriction on his or her acting as a governor, imposed under this Law;
-- (b) is the subject of a disqualification order, or of any other restriction ... under this Law. "Is": the order must bind on the day, first and last days of the period included.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1)(b) the person is the subject of a disqualification order or another restriction` (YMD 2026 6 1) `Orla subject to an order`
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1)(b) the person is the subject of a disqualification order or another restriction` (YMD 2025 1 1) `Orla subject to an order`
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1)(b) the person is the subject of a disqualification order or another restriction` (YMD 2030 12 31) `Orla subject to an order`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(1)(b) the person is the subject of a disqualification order or another restriction` (YMD 2024 12 31) `Orla subject to an order`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(1)(b) the person is the subject of a disqualification order or another restriction` (YMD 2031 1 1) `Orla subject to an order`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(1)(b) the person is the subject of a disqualification order or another restriction` (YMD 2026 6 1) `Orla subject to an order made against somebody else`
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1)(b) the person is the subject of a disqualification order or another restriction` (YMD 2026 6 1) `Rex subject to another restriction under this Law`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(1)(b) the person is the subject of a disqualification order or another restriction` (YMD 2026 6 1) `Ann has nothing reportable`

-- (c) and (d): a disqualification imposed on 1 January 2010 whose last day was 1 January 2015 (the discriminating case of F6.9), one still in force, and one imposed after the day.
`a disqualification elsewhere imposed in 2010, ended in 2015` MEANS `Disqualification elsewhere` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), JUST (YMD 2015 1 1)
`a disqualification elsewhere imposed in 2020, with no end` MEANS `Disqualification elsewhere` OF (YMD 2020 1 1), NOTHING
`a disqualification elsewhere imposed in 2030, with no end` MEANS `Disqualification elsewhere` OF (YMD 2030 1 1), NOTHING
`a disqualification elsewhere whose last day is 1 June 2026` MEANS `Disqualification elsewhere` OF (YMD 2020 1 1), JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)
`Pat once disqualified as a charity trustee` MEANS `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` OF (`Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Pat", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, (LIST `a disqualification elsewhere imposed in 2010, ended in 2015`), EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE
`Pam disqualified as a charity trustee and still so` MEANS `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` OF (`Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Pam", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, (LIST `a disqualification elsewhere imposed in 2020, with no end`), EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE
`Pia to be disqualified as a charity trustee in 2030` MEANS `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` OF (`Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Pia", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, (LIST `a disqualification elsewhere imposed in 2030, with no end`), EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE
`Pip disqualified as a charity trustee until 1 June 2026` MEANS `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` OF (`Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Pip", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, (LIST `a disqualification elsewhere whose last day is 1 June 2026`), EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE
`Dot once disqualified as a company director` MEANS `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` OF (`Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Dot", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, (LIST `a disqualification elsewhere imposed in 2010, ended in 2015`), FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE
`Dan disqualified as a company director and still so` MEANS `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` OF (`Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Dan", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, (LIST `a disqualification elsewhere imposed in 2020, with no end`), FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE

-- src:486 | (c) has been disqualified from or for being a charity trustee or trustee for a charity under the law of any part of the United Kingdom, or from holding any equivalent position under the law of any other jurisdiction;
-- src:487 | (d) has been disqualified from being a company director, or has been made subject to any equivalent disqualification under the law of any jurisdiction other than Jersey;
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1)(c) the person has been disqualified as a charity trustee or from an equivalent position` `the readings taken` (YMD 2026 6 15) `Pat once disqualified as a charity trustee`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(1)(c) the person has been disqualified as a charity trustee or from an equivalent position` (`the readings taken but with F6.9 read as` `only a disqualification still in force counts`) (YMD 2026 6 15) `Pat once disqualified as a charity trustee`
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1)(c) the person has been disqualified as a charity trustee or from an equivalent position` `the readings taken` (YMD 2026 6 15) `Pam disqualified as a charity trustee and still so`
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1)(c) the person has been disqualified as a charity trustee or from an equivalent position` (`the readings taken but with F6.9 read as` `only a disqualification still in force counts`) (YMD 2026 6 15) `Pam disqualified as a charity trustee and still so`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(1)(c) the person has been disqualified as a charity trustee or from an equivalent position` `the readings taken` (YMD 2026 6 15) `Pia to be disqualified as a charity trustee in 2030`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(1)(c) the person has been disqualified as a charity trustee or from an equivalent position` (`the readings taken but with F6.9 read as` `only a disqualification still in force counts`) (YMD 2026 6 15) `Pia to be disqualified as a charity trustee in 2030`
-- The last day of a disqualification is inside it: on 1 June 2026 it still binds, on 2 June 2026 it has ended (visible only on the reading that asks whether it is still in force).
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1)(c) the person has been disqualified as a charity trustee or from an equivalent position` (`the readings taken but with F6.9 read as` `only a disqualification still in force counts`) (YMD 2026 6 1) `Pip disqualified as a charity trustee until 1 June 2026`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(1)(c) the person has been disqualified as a charity trustee or from an equivalent position` (`the readings taken but with F6.9 read as` `only a disqualification still in force counts`) (YMD 2026 6 2) `Pip disqualified as a charity trustee until 1 June 2026`
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1)(c) the person has been disqualified as a charity trustee or from an equivalent position` `the readings taken` (YMD 2026 6 2) `Pip disqualified as a charity trustee until 1 June 2026`
-- (d) is the same for a company director.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1)(d) the person has been disqualified as a company director or from an equivalent position` `the readings taken` (YMD 2026 6 15) `Dot once disqualified as a company director`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(1)(d) the person has been disqualified as a company director or from an equivalent position` (`the readings taken but with F6.9 read as` `only a disqualification still in force counts`) (YMD 2026 6 15) `Dot once disqualified as a company director`
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1)(d) the person has been disqualified as a company director or from an equivalent position` (`the readings taken but with F6.9 read as` `only a disqualification still in force counts`) (YMD 2026 6 15) `Dan disqualified as a company director and still so`
-- A disqualification from the other list is not the other kind.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(1)(d) the person has been disqualified as a company director or from an equivalent position` `the readings taken` (YMD 2026 6 15) `Pat once disqualified as a charity trustee`

`Bob is bankrupt` MEANS `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` OF (`Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Bob", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY, TRUE, EMPTY, FALSE
-- src:488 | (e) is bankrupt or otherwise insolvent, whether under the law of Jersey or elsewhere;
-- (e) is bankrupt or otherwise insolvent, whether under the law of Jersey or elsewhere.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1)(e) the person is bankrupt or otherwise insolvent` `Bob is bankrupt`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(1)(e) the person is bankrupt or otherwise insolvent` `Ann has nothing reportable`

`a spent conviction for an offence under this Law` MEANS `Conviction of a person` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`an unspent conviction for an offence under this Law` MEANS `Conviction of a person` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`an unspent conviction within Article 2(10)(b)` MEANS `Conviction of a person` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`a spent conviction within Article 2(10)(b)` MEANS `Conviction of a person` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`an unspent conviction for an unrelated offence` MEANS `Conviction of a person` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`Cy with only a spent conviction under this Law` MEANS `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` OF (`Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Cy", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY, FALSE, (LIST `a spent conviction for an offence under this Law`), FALSE
`Di with an unspent conviction under this Law` MEANS `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` OF (`Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Di", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY, FALSE, (LIST `an unspent conviction for an offence under this Law`), FALSE
`Ed with an unspent conviction within Article 2(10)(b)` MEANS `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` OF (`Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Ed", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY, FALSE, (LIST `an unspent conviction within Article 2(10)(b)`), FALSE
`Flo with a spent conviction within Article 2(10)(b)` MEANS `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` OF (`Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Flo", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY, FALSE, (LIST `a spent conviction within Article 2(10)(b)`), FALSE
`Gil with an unspent conviction for an unrelated offence` MEANS `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` OF (`Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Gil", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY, FALSE, (LIST `an unspent conviction for an unrelated offence`), FALSE
`Hy within a description prescribed by Order` MEANS `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` OF (`Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Hy", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, TRUE

-- src:489 | (f) has a conviction (whether or not spent) for an offence under this Law;
-- src:490 | (g) has an unspent conviction for an offence falling within Article 2(10)(b); or
-- (f) a conviction (whether or not spent) for an offence under this Law; (g) an UNSPENT conviction for an offence falling within Article 2(10)(b).
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1)(f) the person has a conviction, spent or not, for an offence under this Law` `Cy with only a spent conviction under this Law`
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1)(f) the person has a conviction, spent or not, for an offence under this Law` `Di with an unspent conviction under this Law`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(1)(f) the person has a conviction, spent or not, for an offence under this Law` `Ed with an unspent conviction within Article 2(10)(b)`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(1)(f) the person has a conviction, spent or not, for an offence under this Law` `Gil with an unspent conviction for an unrelated offence`
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1)(g) the person has an unspent conviction for an offence falling within Article 2(10)(b)` `Ed with an unspent conviction within Article 2(10)(b)`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(1)(g) the person has an unspent conviction for an offence falling within Article 2(10)(b)` `Flo with a spent conviction within Article 2(10)(b)`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(1)(g) the person has an unspent conviction for an offence falling within Article 2(10)(b)` `Di with an unspent conviction under this Law`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(1)(g) the person has an unspent conviction for an offence falling within Article 2(10)(b)` `Gil with an unspent conviction for an unrelated offence`
-- src:491 | (h) falls within any other description that may be prescribed by the Minister by Order.[3]
-- (h) any other description prescribed by the Minister by Order.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1)(h) the person falls within another description prescribed by Order` `Hy within a description prescribed by Order`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(1)(h) the person falls within another description prescribed by Order` `Ann has nothing reportable`

-- The list of the descriptions that apply, one test per description, in the order of the paragraph.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1) the reportable matters of the person` `the readings taken` `the notices served` (YMD 2026 6 15) `Abe whose misconduct led to a notice` EQUALS LIST `misconduct as a governor that led to a required steps notice`
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1) the reportable matters of the person` `the readings taken` `the notices served` (YMD 2026 6 15) `Orla subject to an order` EQUALS LIST `a disqualification order or other restriction on acting as a governor imposed under this Law`
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1) the reportable matters of the person` `the readings taken` `the notices served` (YMD 2026 6 15) `Pat once disqualified as a charity trustee` EQUALS LIST `disqualification as a charity trustee under the law of the United Kingdom or an equivalent position elsewhere`
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1) the reportable matters of the person` `the readings taken` `the notices served` (YMD 2026 6 15) `Dot once disqualified as a company director` EQUALS LIST `disqualification as a company director, or an equivalent disqualification outside Jersey`
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1) the reportable matters of the person` `the readings taken` `the notices served` (YMD 2026 6 15) `Bob is bankrupt` EQUALS LIST `bankruptcy or other insolvency`
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1) the reportable matters of the person` `the readings taken` `the notices served` (YMD 2026 6 15) `Cy with only a spent conviction under this Law` EQUALS LIST `a conviction, whether or not spent, for an offence under this Law`
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1) the reportable matters of the person` `the readings taken` `the notices served` (YMD 2026 6 15) `Ed with an unspent conviction within Article 2(10)(b)` EQUALS LIST `an unspent conviction for an offence falling within Article 2(10)(b)`
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1) the reportable matters of the person` `the readings taken` `the notices served` (YMD 2026 6 15) `Hy within a description prescribed by Order` EQUALS LIST `a description prescribed by Order`
#ASSERT       null (`Art 19(1) the reportable matters of the person` `the readings taken` `the notices served` (YMD 2026 6 15) `Ann has nothing reportable`)
#ASSERT       null (`Art 19(1) the reportable matters of the person` `the readings taken` `the notices served` (YMD 2026 6 15) `Gil with an unspent conviction for an unrelated offence`)
-- A person with two matters has both, in the order of the paragraph: (f) and (g) for an unspent conviction under this Law that is also within Article 2(10)(b).
`Ivo with one unspent conviction under this Law that is also within Article 2(10)(b), and bankrupt` MEANS `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` OF (`Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Ivo", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY, TRUE, (LIST (`Conviction of a person` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)), FALSE
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1) the reportable matters of the person` `the readings taken` `the notices served` (YMD 2026 6 15) `Ivo with one unspent conviction under this Law that is also within Article 2(10)(b), and bankrupt` EQUALS LIST `bankruptcy or other insolvency`, `a conviction, whether or not spent, for an offence under this Law`, `an unspent conviction for an offence falling within Article 2(10)(b)`
-- The power behind (h): the Minister may prescribe a description by Order.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(1)(h) the Minister may prescribe a further description of reportable matter by Order` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `prescribe by Order a description of reportable matter` `the Minister` AT 10
-- EXPECT: STANDING prescribe by Order a description of reportable matter
#TRACE `Art 19(1)(h) the Minister may prescribe a further description of reportable matter by Order` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

§§ `Article 19(2) -- the duty to report`

`Gus's position: the matter arose on 1 March 2026, he became aware on 20 March, and reported to both on 25 March` MEANS `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 3 20), JUST (YMD 2026 3 25), JUST (YMD 2026 3 25), TRUE, FALSE
`Gus's position: the matter arose on 1 March 2026 and he reported to both on 11 March, ten days later` MEANS `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 3 1), JUST (YMD 2026 3 11), JUST (YMD 2026 3 11), FALSE, FALSE
`Gus's position: the matter arose on 1 March 2026 and he reported to both on 12 March, eleven days later` MEANS `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 3 1), JUST (YMD 2026 3 12), JUST (YMD 2026 3 12), FALSE, FALSE
`Gus's position: arose on 1 March 2026, unreported` MEANS `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 3 1), NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, TRUE
`Gus's position: arose on 1 March 2026, unreported, the prompt time not yet run out` MEANS `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 3 1), NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE
`Gus's position: arose on 1 March 2026, reported only to the Commissioner on 3 March` MEANS `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 3 1), NOTHING, JUST (YMD 2026 3 3), TRUE, TRUE
`ten days` MEANS JUST 10
`the number of days not given` MEANS NOTHING

-- src:492 | (2) A governor of an entity applying for registration, or of a registered charity, must report any reportable matter promptly to that entity or charity and to the Commissioner.
-- Promptness (F6.12). The words are "must report any reportable matter promptly": the Law gives no number of days.
-- Reading taken: promptness is a determination the caller supplies. The matter arose on 1 March and the governor became aware on 20 March, and reported on 25 March.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(2) the report made on the date is prompt` `the readings taken` `the number of days not given` `Gus's position: the matter arose on 1 March 2026, he became aware on 20 March, and reported to both on 25 March` (YMD 2026 3 25)
-- Counting from the matter arising, with ten days as the longest prompt interval: 24 days is not prompt. Counting from awareness: 5 days is prompt.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(2) the report made on the date is prompt` (`the readings taken but with F6.12 read as` `promptness is a number of days from the matter arising`) `ten days` `Gus's position: the matter arose on 1 March 2026, he became aware on 20 March, and reported to both on 25 March` (YMD 2026 3 25)
#ASSERT       `Art 19(2) the report made on the date is prompt` (`the readings taken but with F6.12 read as` `promptness is a number of days from the governor becoming aware of the matter`) `ten days` `Gus's position: the matter arose on 1 March 2026, he became aware on 20 March, and reported to both on 25 March` (YMD 2026 3 25)
-- The boundary on both sides, from the matter arising: ten days is prompt, eleven is not.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(2) the report made on the date is prompt` (`the readings taken but with F6.12 read as` `promptness is a number of days from the matter arising`) `ten days` `Gus's position: the matter arose on 1 March 2026 and he reported to both on 11 March, ten days later` (YMD 2026 3 11)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(2) the report made on the date is prompt` (`the readings taken but with F6.12 read as` `promptness is a number of days from the matter arising`) `ten days` `Gus's position: the matter arose on 1 March 2026 and he reported to both on 12 March, eleven days later` (YMD 2026 3 12)
-- A reading that counts days has nothing to count with if the caller gives no number: the Law gives none.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 19(2) the report made on the date is prompt` (`the readings taken but with F6.12 read as` `promptness is a number of days from the matter arising`) `the number of days not given` `Gus's position: the matter arose on 1 March 2026, he became aware on 20 March, and reported to both on 25 March` (YMD 2026 3 25)
-- Complied with paragraph (2): both reports made, both prompt.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(2) the governor has complied with paragraph (2)` `the readings taken` `the number of days not given` `Gus's position: the matter arose on 1 March 2026, he became aware on 20 March, and reported to both on 25 March`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(2) the governor has complied with paragraph (2)` `the readings taken` `the number of days not given` `Gus's position: arose on 1 March 2026, reported only to the Commissioner on 3 March`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(2) the governor has complied with paragraph (2)` (`the readings taken but with F6.12 read as` `promptness is a number of days from the matter arising`) `ten days` `Gus's position: the matter arose on 1 March 2026, he became aware on 20 March, and reported to both on 25 March`
#ASSERT       `Art 19(2) the governor has complied with paragraph (2)` (`the readings taken but with F6.12 read as` `promptness is a number of days from the governor becoming aware of the matter`) `ten days` `Gus's position: the matter arose on 1 March 2026, he became aware on 20 March, and reported to both on 25 March`

-- In breach of paragraph (2) on a day: the matter is unreported (to either) and the time for a prompt report has run out. No reportable matter, no breach.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(2) the governor is in breach of paragraph (2)` `the readings taken` `the number of days not given` (YMD 2026 3 20) `Gus with a reportable matter` `Gus's position: arose on 1 March 2026, unreported`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(2) the governor is in breach of paragraph (2)` `the readings taken` `the number of days not given` (YMD 2026 3 20) `Gus with a reportable matter` `Gus's position: arose on 1 March 2026, unreported, the prompt time not yet run out`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(2) the governor is in breach of paragraph (2)` `the readings taken` `the number of days not given` (YMD 2026 3 20) `Gwen with no reportable matter` `Gus's position: arose on 1 March 2026, unreported`
-- Reported to the Commissioner only: still in breach, as the report to the entity or charity is missing.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(2) the governor is in breach of paragraph (2)` `the readings taken` `the number of days not given` (YMD 2026 3 20) `Gus with a reportable matter` `Gus's position: arose on 1 March 2026, reported only to the Commissioner on 3 March`
-- Both reported (late): no longer in breach on later days.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(2) the governor is in breach of paragraph (2)` `the readings taken` `the number of days not given` (YMD 2026 3 26) `Gus with a reportable matter` `Gus's position: the matter arose on 1 March 2026, he became aware on 20 March, and reported to both on 25 March`
-- The counting readings. Matter arose 1 March: the last prompt day is 11 March (ten days), so the governor is in breach from 12 March, and not on 11 March.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(2) the governor is in breach of paragraph (2)` (`the readings taken but with F6.12 read as` `promptness is a number of days from the matter arising`) `ten days` (YMD 2026 3 12) `Gus with a reportable matter` `Gus's position: arose on 1 March 2026, unreported`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(2) the governor is in breach of paragraph (2)` (`the readings taken but with F6.12 read as` `promptness is a number of days from the matter arising`) `ten days` (YMD 2026 3 11) `Gus with a reportable matter` `Gus's position: arose on 1 March 2026, unreported`

-- The duty. Both reports are due, to the entity or charity and to the Commissioner.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(2) the governor must report the reportable matter` TRUE `a registered charity entity` `Gus with a reportable matter` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `report the reportable matter to the entity or charity` `a governor` AT 3
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `report the reportable matter to the Commissioner` `a governor` AT 4
-- Only the report to the Commissioner has been made: the report to the entity or charity stands.
-- EXPECT: STANDING report the reportable matter to the entity or charity
#TRACE `Art 19(2) the governor must report the reportable matter` TRUE `a registered charity entity` `Gus with a reportable matter` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `report the reportable matter to the Commissioner` `a governor` AT 4
-- An entity applying for registration: the governor owes the same reports.
-- EXPECT: STANDING report the reportable matter to the Commissioner
#TRACE `Art 19(2) the governor must report the reportable matter` FALSE `an entity applying for registration` `Gus with a reportable matter` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `report the reportable matter to the entity or charity` `a governor` AT 3
-- A governor with no reportable matter has nothing to report.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(2) the governor must report the reportable matter` TRUE `a registered charity entity` `Gwen with no reportable matter` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- An entity that is neither applying nor registered: no governor of such an entity owes a report.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(2) the governor must report the reportable matter` FALSE `an entity not on the register` `Gus with a reportable matter` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

§§ `Article 19(3) -- the declaration before the application is made`

-- src:493 | (3) A governor of an entity applying for registration must, if there is no reportable matter in relation to that governor, provide to the entity a declaration to that effect before the application is made.
-- (3) must, if there is no reportable matter, provide to the entity a declaration to that effect before the application is made. Application made on 10 May 2026.
-- The day of the application itself: in time on the reading taken (a declaration given that day, before the application was made); out of time on the other.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(3) the declaration was provided before the application was made` `the readings taken` (JUST (YMD 2026 5 10)) (YMD 2026 5 10)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(3) the declaration was provided before the application was made` (`the readings taken but with F6.20 read as` `a declaration must be given on an earlier day than the application`) (JUST (YMD 2026 5 10)) (YMD 2026 5 10)
-- The day before: in time on both readings. The day after: out of time on both. No declaration: not in time.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(3) the declaration was provided before the application was made` `the readings taken` (JUST (YMD 2026 5 9)) (YMD 2026 5 10)
#ASSERT       `Art 19(3) the declaration was provided before the application was made` (`the readings taken but with F6.20 read as` `a declaration must be given on an earlier day than the application`) (JUST (YMD 2026 5 9)) (YMD 2026 5 10)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(3) the declaration was provided before the application was made` `the readings taken` (JUST (YMD 2026 5 11)) (YMD 2026 5 10)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(3) the declaration was provided before the application was made` (`the readings taken but with F6.20 read as` `a declaration must be given on an earlier day than the application`) (JUST (YMD 2026 5 11)) (YMD 2026 5 10)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(3) the declaration was provided before the application was made` `the readings taken` NOTHING (YMD 2026 5 10)
-- The duty on the date-serial clock; the last day for the declaration is the day of the application (reading taken) or the day before.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(3) the governor of an applicant must provide a declaration of no reportable matter` `the readings taken` `an entity applying for registration` `Gwen with no reportable matter` (YMD 2026 5 10) AT (Day (YMD 2026 5 1)) WITH
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `provide a declaration that there is no reportable matter` `a governor` AT (Day (YMD 2026 5 10))
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 19(3)
#TRACE `Art 19(3) the governor of an applicant must provide a declaration of no reportable matter` `the readings taken` `an entity applying for registration` `Gwen with no reportable matter` (YMD 2026 5 10) AT (Day (YMD 2026 5 1)) WITH
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `provide a declaration that there is no reportable matter` `a governor` AT (Day (YMD 2026 5 11))
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 19(3)
#TRACE `Art 19(3) the governor of an applicant must provide a declaration of no reportable matter` (`the readings taken but with F6.20 read as` `a declaration must be given on an earlier day than the application`) `an entity applying for registration` `Gwen with no reportable matter` (YMD 2026 5 10) AT (Day (YMD 2026 5 1)) WITH
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `provide a declaration that there is no reportable matter` `a governor` AT (Day (YMD 2026 5 10))
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(3) the governor of an applicant must provide a declaration of no reportable matter` (`the readings taken but with F6.20 read as` `a declaration must be given on an earlier day than the application`) `an entity applying for registration` `Gwen with no reportable matter` (YMD 2026 5 10) AT (Day (YMD 2026 5 1)) WITH
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `provide a declaration that there is no reportable matter` `a governor` AT (Day (YMD 2026 5 9))
-- Nothing done and the closing day passed: the duty is breached.
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 19(3)
#TRACE `Art 19(3) the governor of an applicant must provide a declaration of no reportable matter` `the readings taken` `an entity applying for registration` `Gwen with no reportable matter` (YMD 2026 5 10) AT (Day (YMD 2026 5 1)) WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` (Day (YMD 2026 5 11)))
-- A governor with a reportable matter owes no declaration; an entity not applying gives no duty.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(3) the governor of an applicant must provide a declaration of no reportable matter` `the readings taken` `an entity applying for registration` `Gus with a reportable matter` (YMD 2026 5 10) AT (Day (YMD 2026 5 1)) WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` (Day (YMD 2026 5 11)))
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(3) the governor of an applicant must provide a declaration of no reportable matter` `the readings taken` `a registered charity entity` `Gwen with no reportable matter` (YMD 2026 5 10) AT (Day (YMD 2026 5 1)) WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` (Day (YMD 2026 5 11)))

§§ `Article 19(4) -- the declaration when notified`

`Gwen: notified on 1 June 2026, no declaration yet` MEANS `Position of a governor under Article 19(4)` OF (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)), NOTHING, FALSE
`Gwen: notified on 1 June 2026, declaration provided on 2 June` MEANS `Position of a governor under Article 19(4)` OF (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)), (JUST (YMD 2026 6 2)), FALSE
`Gwen: notified on 1 June 2026, declaration provided on 1 June` MEANS `Position of a governor under Article 19(4)` OF (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)), (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)), FALSE
`Gwen: notified on 1 June 2026, no declaration yet, a reasonable time has passed` MEANS `Position of a governor under Article 19(4)` OF (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)), NOTHING, TRUE
`Gwen: never notified` MEANS `Position of a governor under Article 19(4)` OF NOTHING, NOTHING, TRUE

-- src:494 | (4) A governor of a registered charity must, if there is no reportable matter in relation to that governor, provide to the charity a declaration to that effect when notified by the charity that it is preparing its annual return.
-- (4) must, if there is no reportable matter, provide to the charity a declaration to that effect when notified by the charity that it is preparing its annual return.
-- Reading taken: the declaration is due on the day of the notification, so the governor is in breach from the next day. The day of the notification itself is not a breach.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(4) the governor is in breach of paragraph (4)` `the readings taken` TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) `Gwen with no reportable matter` `Gwen: notified on 1 June 2026, no declaration yet`
#ASSERT       `Art 19(4) the governor is in breach of paragraph (4)` `the readings taken` TRUE (YMD 2026 6 2) `Gwen with no reportable matter` `Gwen: notified on 1 June 2026, no declaration yet`
-- Provided on 2 June: in breach on none of the days up to and including 2 June (it was provided by then), and on none after.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(4) the governor is in breach of paragraph (4)` `the readings taken` TRUE (YMD 2026 6 2) `Gwen with no reportable matter` `Gwen: notified on 1 June 2026, declaration provided on 2 June`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(4) the governor is in breach of paragraph (4)` `the readings taken` TRUE (YMD 2026 6 9) `Gwen with no reportable matter` `Gwen: notified on 1 June 2026, declaration provided on 2 June`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(4) the governor is in breach of paragraph (4)` `the readings taken` TRUE (YMD 2026 6 9) `Gwen with no reportable matter` `Gwen: notified on 1 June 2026, declaration provided on 1 June`
-- Never notified: no duty has arisen. A governor with a reportable matter is not within paragraph (4). An entity that is not a registered charity is not within it either.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(4) the governor is in breach of paragraph (4)` `the readings taken` TRUE (YMD 2026 6 9) `Gwen with no reportable matter` `Gwen: never notified`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(4) the governor is in breach of paragraph (4)` `the readings taken` TRUE (YMD 2026 6 9) `Gus with a reportable matter` `Gwen: notified on 1 June 2026, no declaration yet`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(4) the governor is in breach of paragraph (4)` `the readings taken` FALSE (YMD 2026 6 9) `Gwen with no reportable matter` `Gwen: notified on 1 June 2026, no declaration yet`
-- F6.21, the other reading: a reasonable time is allowed. On the day of the notification, with a reasonable time not passed, not in breach; once a reasonable time has passed, in breach.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(4) the governor is in breach of paragraph (4)` (`the readings taken but with F6.21 read as` `the governor is in breach once a reasonable time has passed after the notification`) TRUE (YMD 2026 6 2) `Gwen with no reportable matter` `Gwen: notified on 1 June 2026, no declaration yet`
#ASSERT       `Art 19(4) the governor is in breach of paragraph (4)` (`the readings taken but with F6.21 read as` `the governor is in breach once a reasonable time has passed after the notification`) TRUE (YMD 2026 6 9) `Gwen with no reportable matter` `Gwen: notified on 1 June 2026, no declaration yet, a reasonable time has passed`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(4) the governor is in breach of paragraph (4)` (`the readings taken but with F6.21 read as` `the governor is in breach once a reasonable time has passed after the notification`) TRUE (YMD 2026 6 9) `Gwen with no reportable matter` `Gwen: never notified`
-- The duty, from the notification: due the same day on the reading taken; a standing duty on the other.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(4) the governor of a registered charity must provide a declaration of no reportable matter` `the readings taken` TRUE `Gwen with no reportable matter` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `provide a declaration that there is no reportable matter` `a governor` AT 0
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 19(4)
#TRACE `Art 19(4) the governor of a registered charity must provide a declaration of no reportable matter` `the readings taken` TRUE `Gwen with no reportable matter` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 1)
-- EXPECT: STANDING provide a declaration that there is no reportable matter
#TRACE `Art 19(4) the governor of a registered charity must provide a declaration of no reportable matter` (`the readings taken but with F6.21 read as` `the governor is in breach once a reasonable time has passed after the notification`) TRUE `Gwen with no reportable matter` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(4) the governor of a registered charity must provide a declaration of no reportable matter` (`the readings taken but with F6.21 read as` `the governor is in breach once a reasonable time has passed after the notification`) TRUE `Gwen with no reportable matter` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `provide a declaration that there is no reportable matter` `a governor` AT 30
-- No notification yet, a governor with a reportable matter, or an entity that is not a registered charity: nothing is owed.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(4) the governor of a registered charity must provide a declaration of no reportable matter` `the readings taken` TRUE `Gwen with no reportable matter` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 5)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(4) the governor of a registered charity must provide a declaration of no reportable matter` `the readings taken` TRUE `Gus with a reportable matter` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 5)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(4) the governor of a registered charity must provide a declaration of no reportable matter` `the readings taken` FALSE `Gwen with no reportable matter` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 5)

§§ `Article 19(5), (6) and (7) -- the statement that declarations are held`

`Hal who has reported` MEANS `Position of a governor for Article 19(5)` OF "Hal", TRUE, FALSE
`Ida who has declared` MEANS `Position of a governor for Article 19(5)` OF "Ida", FALSE, TRUE
`Jo who has neither reported nor declared` MEANS `Position of a governor for Article 19(5)` OF "Jo", FALSE, FALSE
`Kit who has both reported and declared` MEANS `Position of a governor for Article 19(5)` OF "Kit", TRUE, TRUE

-- src:495 | (5) The entity must state in its application, and the registered charity must state in its annual return, that it has declarations from all of its governors who have not made a report under paragraph (2).
-- (5) The entity must state in its application, and the registered charity in its annual return, that it has declarations from all of its governors who have not made a report under paragraph (2).
-- A governor who has reported needs no declaration; every other governor must have given one.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(5) the applicant has stated that it holds declarations from all its governors who have not reported` TRUE (LIST `Hal who has reported`, `Ida who has declared`)
#ASSERT       `Art 19(5) the applicant has stated that it holds declarations from all its governors who have not reported` TRUE (LIST `Kit who has both reported and declared`)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(5) the applicant has stated that it holds declarations from all its governors who have not reported` TRUE (LIST `Hal who has reported`, `Jo who has neither reported nor declared`)
-- No statement in the application: the entity has not complied, however many declarations it holds.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(5) the applicant has stated that it holds declarations from all its governors who have not reported` FALSE (LIST `Hal who has reported`, `Ida who has declared`)
-- No governors at all: the statement is vacuously true.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(5) the applicant has stated that it holds declarations from all its governors who have not reported` TRUE EMPTY
-- The same for a registered charity's annual return.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(5) the registered charity has stated in its annual return that it holds declarations` TRUE (LIST `Hal who has reported`, `Ida who has declared`)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(5) the registered charity has stated in its annual return that it holds declarations` TRUE (LIST `Jo who has neither reported nor declared`)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(5) the registered charity has stated in its annual return that it holds declarations` FALSE (LIST `Ida who has declared`)

-- src:496 | (6) An application for registration is not complete if the entity has not complied with paragraph (5).
-- (6) An application for registration is not complete if the entity has not complied with paragraph (5).
#ASSERT       `Art 19(6) the application is not complete for want of Article 19(5)` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(6) the application is not complete for want of Article 19(5)` TRUE

-- The duty: the applicant states in its application; a registered charity in its annual return.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(5) the entity must state that it holds declarations` `an entity applying for registration` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an applicant for registration` DOES `state that the entity holds declarations from all its governors who have not made a report` `an applicant for registration` AT 7
-- EXPECT: STANDING state that the entity holds declarations
#TRACE `Art 19(5) the entity must state that it holds declarations` `an entity applying for registration` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(5) the entity must state that it holds declarations` `a registered charity entity` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `state that the entity holds declarations from all its governors who have not made a report` `a registered charity` AT 7

-- src:497 | (7) A registered charity that contravenes paragraph (5) must explain to the Commissioner the reason for the contravention.
-- (7) A registered charity that contravenes paragraph (5) must explain to the Commissioner the reason for the contravention.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(7) the registered charity that contravenes paragraph (5) must explain the reason to the Commissioner` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `explain to the Commissioner the reason for contravening paragraph (5)` `a registered charity` AT 20
-- EXPECT: STANDING explain to the Commissioner
#TRACE `Art 19(7) the registered charity that contravenes paragraph (5) must explain the reason to the Commissioner` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- Where the charity complied, nothing is owed.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(7) the registered charity that contravenes paragraph (5) must explain the reason to the Commissioner` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

§§ `Article 19(8) -- no acting as a governor while in breach of paragraph (2) or (4)`

-- src:498 | (8) A person must not act as a governor of a registered charity at any time when the person is in breach of paragraph (2) or (4).
-- (8) A person must not act as a governor of a registered charity at any time when the person is in breach of paragraph (2) or (4).
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 19(8)
#TRACE `Art 19(8) the person must not act as a governor while in breach of Article 19(2) or (4)` TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `any person` DOES `act as a governor of a registered charity` `any person` AT 5
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 19(8)
#TRACE `Art 19(8) the person must not act as a governor while in breach of Article 19(2) or (4)` TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `any person` DOES `act as a governor of a registered charity` `any person` AT 5
-- In breach of neither: acting is not prohibited by paragraph (8).
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(8) the person must not act as a governor while in breach of Article 19(2) or (4)` TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `any person` DOES `act as a governor of a registered charity` `any person` AT 5
-- Not a registered charity: not the prohibition of this paragraph.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(8) the person must not act as a governor while in breach of Article 19(2) or (4)` FALSE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `any person` DOES `act as a governor of a registered charity` `any person` AT 5
-- The prohibition stands while the person is in breach and has not acted.
-- EXPECT: STANDING act as a governor of a registered charity
#TRACE `Art 19(8) the person must not act as a governor while in breach of Article 19(2) or (4)` TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- No offence is attached to paragraph (8) on the reading taken (F6.11); on the other reading the penalty of paragraph (11) is attached.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(8) the penalty for contravening Article 19(8)` `the readings taken` EQUALS `Penalty provided` OF NOTHING, `no fine is provided`
#ASSERT       `Art 19(8) the penalty for contravening Article 19(8)` (`the readings taken but with F6.11 read as` `Article 19(11) reaches paragraph (8) as well`) EQUALS `Penalty provided` OF (JUST 12), `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`

§§ `Article 19(9) -- what the Commissioner does when a governor reports to the Commissioner`

-- Positional construction of a report: the governor reported to the Commissioner; the Commissioner has applied to the court; the issue has been determined; any resulting order or notice has been complied with.
`a report to the Commissioner, the issue not yet determined` MEANS `Reported matter under Article 19(9)` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`a report to the Commissioner, determined and complied with` MEANS `Reported matter under Article 19(9)` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`a report to the Commissioner, determined but the resulting notice not complied with` MEANS `Reported matter under Article 19(9)` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`a report to the Commissioner, referred to the court, not yet determined` MEANS `Reported matter under Article 19(9)` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`no report to the Commissioner` MEANS `Reported matter under Article 19(9)` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

-- src:499 | (9) If a governor reports a reportable matter to the Commissioner, the Commissioner –
-- src:500 | (a) must make inquiries to determine whether the governor is a fit and proper person to be a governor;
-- (a) must make inquiries to determine whether the governor is a fit and proper person. No period is stated.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(a) the Commissioner must make inquiries into whether the governor is a fit and proper person` `a report to the Commissioner, the issue not yet determined` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `make inquiries to determine whether the governor is a fit and proper person` `the Commissioner` AT 30
-- EXPECT: STANDING make inquiries to determine whether the governor is a fit and proper person
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(a) the Commissioner must make inquiries into whether the governor is a fit and proper person` `a report to the Commissioner, the issue not yet determined` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- Where no report has been made to the Commissioner, nothing is owed.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(a) the Commissioner must make inquiries into whether the governor is a fit and proper person` `no report to the Commissioner` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

-- src:501 | (b) may apply to the court to determine that issue under Article 20;
-- (b) may apply to the court to determine that issue under Article 20.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(b) the Commissioner may apply to the court to determine the issue` `a report to the Commissioner, the issue not yet determined` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `apply to the court to determine whether the governor is a fit and proper person` `the Commissioner` AT 30
-- A permission left unused is not a breach: it stands.
-- EXPECT: STANDING apply to the court to determine whether the governor is a fit and proper person
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(b) the Commissioner may apply to the court to determine the issue` `a report to the Commissioner, the issue not yet determined` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(b) the Commissioner may apply to the court to determine the issue` `no report to the Commissioner` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

-- src:502 | (c) must not, in the case of an application for registration, grant that application until the issue has been determined and any resulting order or notice complied with;
-- (c) must not, in the case of an application for registration, grant that application until the issue has been determined and any resulting order or notice complied with.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` (LIST `a report to the Commissioner, the issue not yet determined`)
#ASSERT       `Art 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` (LIST `a report to the Commissioner, determined but the resulting notice not complied with`)
#ASSERT       `Art 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` (LIST `a report to the Commissioner, referred to the court, not yet determined`)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` (LIST `a report to the Commissioner, determined and complied with`)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` (LIST `no report to the Commissioner`)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` EMPTY
-- One governor's open report bars the grant even if another's is closed.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` (LIST `a report to the Commissioner, determined and complied with`, `a report to the Commissioner, the issue not yet determined`)
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 19(9)(c)
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(c) the Commissioner must not grant the application` `an entity applying for registration` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `grant the application for registration` `the Commissioner` AT 9
-- EXPECT: STANDING grant the application for registration
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(c) the Commissioner must not grant the application` `an entity applying for registration` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(c) the Commissioner must not grant the application` `an entity applying for registration` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `grant the application for registration` `the Commissioner` AT 9
-- The bar is for an application for registration: a registered charity has nothing to be granted.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(c) the Commissioner must not grant the application` `a registered charity entity` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `grant the application for registration` `the Commissioner` AT 9

-- src:503 | (d) may, in the case of a registered charity, by written notice to the charity, permit, either unconditionally or subject to any condition appearing to the Commissioner to be necessary, the governor to act as a governor until that issue is determined or the notice is withdrawn;
-- (d) may, in the case of a registered charity, by written notice to the charity, permit the governor to act as a governor until that issue is determined or the notice is withdrawn.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(d) the Commissioner may permit the governor to act until the issue is determined` TRUE `a report to the Commissioner, the issue not yet determined` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `permit the governor to act as a governor until the issue is determined or the notice is withdrawn` `the Commissioner` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING permit the governor to act as a governor until the issue is determined
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(d) the Commissioner may permit the governor to act until the issue is determined` TRUE `a report to the Commissioner, the issue not yet determined` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- An applicant is not a registered charity: no such permission is given by (d).
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(d) the Commissioner may permit the governor to act until the issue is determined` FALSE `a report to the Commissioner, the issue not yet determined` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

-- src:504 | (e) must, if the issue is not to be determined by the court under sub-paragraph (b), on determining the issue –
-- src:505 | (i) notify the entity that the application will be refused unless the governor is removed, or in the case of a registered charity serve a required steps notice requiring the charity to suspend or remove the governor, or
-- src:506 | (ii) by notice in writing, entered in the register, give permission for the governor to act as a governor, either unconditionally or subject to any condition or time limit that appears to the Commissioner to be necessary.
-- (e) must, if the issue is not to be determined by the court under sub-paragraph (b), on determining the issue, (i) notify the entity that the application will be refused unless the governor is removed,
-- or in the case of a registered charity serve a required steps notice requiring the charity to suspend or remove the governor, or (ii) give permission by notice entered in the register.
-- An application: notify, or permit.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(e) the Commissioner must remove or permit on determining the issue` `the readings taken` `an entity applying for registration` `the register entry of an ordinary charity` `a report to the Commissioner, the issue not yet determined` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `notify the entity that the application will be refused unless the governor is removed` `the Commissioner` AT 5
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(e) the Commissioner must remove or permit on determining the issue` `the readings taken` `an entity applying for registration` `the register entry of an ordinary charity` `a report to the Commissioner, the issue not yet determined` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `give permission for the governor to act as a governor by notice entered in the register` `the Commissioner` AT 5
-- A required steps notice is for a registered charity, not for an application: it does not discharge the duty.
-- EXPECT: STANDING notify the entity that the application will be refused unless the governor is removed
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(e) the Commissioner must remove or permit on determining the issue` `the readings taken` `an entity applying for registration` `the register entry of an ordinary charity` `a report to the Commissioner, the issue not yet determined` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `serve a required steps notice requiring the charity to suspend or remove the governor` `the Commissioner` AT 5
-- A registered charity: serve a required steps notice, or permit.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(e) the Commissioner must remove or permit on determining the issue` `the readings taken` `a registered charity entity` `the register entry of an ordinary charity` `a report to the Commissioner, the issue not yet determined` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `serve a required steps notice requiring the charity to suspend or remove the governor` `the Commissioner` AT 5
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(e) the Commissioner must remove or permit on determining the issue` `the readings taken` `a registered charity entity` `the register entry of an ordinary charity` `a report to the Commissioner, the issue not yet determined` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `give permission for the governor to act as a governor by notice entered in the register` `the Commissioner` AT 5
-- EXPECT: STANDING serve a required steps notice requiring the charity to suspend or remove the governor
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(e) the Commissioner must remove or permit on determining the issue` `the readings taken` `a registered charity entity` `the register entry of an ordinary charity` `a report to the Commissioner, the issue not yet determined` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- Trap T11, F6.15: an organized religious charity. Reading taken: Article 28(3) prevails, so only the permission remains; serving the notice does not discharge the duty.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(e) the Commissioner must remove or permit on determining the issue` `the readings taken` `a registered charity entity` `the register entry of an organized religious charity` `a report to the Commissioner, the issue not yet determined` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `give permission for the governor to act as a governor by notice entered in the register` `the Commissioner` AT 5
-- EXPECT: STANDING give permission for the governor to act as a governor by notice entered in the register
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(e) the Commissioner must remove or permit on determining the issue` `the readings taken` `a registered charity entity` `the register entry of an organized religious charity` `a report to the Commissioner, the issue not yet determined` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `serve a required steps notice requiring the charity to suspend or remove the governor` `the Commissioner` AT 5
-- The other reading (B): the duty stands, so serving the notice discharges it.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(e) the Commissioner must remove or permit on determining the issue` (`the readings taken but with F6.15 read as` `the duty stands and the notice is void to the extent that it requires removal`) `a registered charity entity` `the register entry of an organized religious charity` `a report to the Commissioner, the issue not yet determined` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `serve a required steps notice requiring the charity to suspend or remove the governor` `the Commissioner` AT 5
-- The third reading (C): the two provisions conflict and the Law does not say which prevails. The question has no answer.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 19(9)(e)(i) the removal alternative of the Commissioner` (`the readings taken but with F6.15 read as` `the two provisions conflict and the Law does not say which prevails`) `a registered charity entity` `the register entry of an organized religious charity`
-- ... but only for the organized religious charity: an ordinary registered charity has no conflict.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(e) the Commissioner must remove or permit on determining the issue` (`the readings taken but with F6.15 read as` `the two provisions conflict and the Law does not say which prevails`) `a registered charity entity` `the register entry of an ordinary charity` `a report to the Commissioner, the issue not yet determined` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `serve a required steps notice requiring the charity to suspend or remove the governor` `the Commissioner` AT 5
-- If the issue is to be determined by the court, the Commissioner's duty under (e) does not arise.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(e) the Commissioner must remove or permit on determining the issue` `the readings taken` `a registered charity entity` `the register entry of an ordinary charity` `a report to the Commissioner, referred to the court, not yet determined` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- No report to the Commissioner: nothing to determine.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(9)(e) the Commissioner must remove or permit on determining the issue` `the readings taken` `a registered charity entity` `the register entry of an ordinary charity` `no report to the Commissioner` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

§§ `Article 19(10), (11) and (12) -- acting as a governor after reporting; the offence`

-- Positional construction of a governor's position: the matter arose on; became aware on; reported to the entity or charity on; reported to the Commissioner on; the reports were prompt; a prompt time has run out.
`position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` MEANS `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 3 1), JUST (YMD 2026 3 12), JUST (YMD 2026 3 10), TRUE, FALSE
`position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner only, on 10 March` MEANS `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 3 1), NOTHING, JUST (YMD 2026 3 10), TRUE, FALSE
`position of Gus: reported to the charity only, on 12 March` MEANS `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 3 1), JUST (YMD 2026 3 12), NOTHING, TRUE, FALSE
`position of Gus: reported to nobody` MEANS `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 3 1), NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, TRUE

-- Positional construction of a permission: source; given on; withdrawn on; the issue is determined on; time limit ends on.
`a permission under Article 19(9)(d) given on 1 April 2026` MEANS `Permission to act as a governor` OF `the Commissioner by written notice to the charity under Article 19(9)(d)`, (YMD 2026 4 1), NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING
`a permission under Article 19(9)(e)(ii) given on 1 April 2026 with a time limit ending on 31 May` MEANS `Permission to act as a governor` OF `the Commissioner by notice entered in the register under Article 19(9)(e)(ii)`, (YMD 2026 4 1), NOTHING, NOTHING, JUST (YMD 2026 5 31)
`a permission under Article 19(9)(d) given on 1 April 2026 and withdrawn on 15 May` MEANS `Permission to act as a governor` OF `the Commissioner by written notice to the charity under Article 19(9)(d)`, (YMD 2026 4 1), JUST (YMD 2026 5 15), NOTHING, NOTHING
`a permission under Article 19(9)(d) given on 1 April 2026 until the issue is determined on 20 May` MEANS `Permission to act as a governor` OF `the Commissioner by written notice to the charity under Article 19(9)(d)`, (YMD 2026 4 1), NOTHING, JUST (YMD 2026 5 20), NOTHING
`a permission by the court given on 1 April 2026` MEANS `Permission to act as a governor` OF `the court by an order under Article 20`, (YMD 2026 4 1), NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING

-- src:507 | (10) A person must not act as a governor of a registered charity at any time after reporting a reportable matter, unless the governor –
-- (10) A person must not act as a governor of a registered charity at any time after reporting a reportable matter, unless the governor (a) is permitted ... and (b) acts in accordance with any condition.
-- F6.10, when the ban starts. Reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March. The day of the report is inside the ban.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` EMPTY (YMD 2026 3 9) TRUE
#ASSERT       `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` EMPTY (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE
#ASSERT       `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` EMPTY (YMD 2026 3 13) TRUE
-- Reported to the charity only: no ban yet on the reading taken, a ban from 12 March on the reading that starts with the report to the charity.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the charity only, on 12 March` EMPTY (YMD 2026 3 13) TRUE
#ASSERT       `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` (`the readings taken but with F6.10 read as` `the ban starts on the report to the entity or charity`) TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the charity only, on 12 March` EMPTY (YMD 2026 3 13) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` (`the readings taken but with F6.10 read as` `the ban starts on the report to the entity or charity`) TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the charity only, on 12 March` EMPTY (YMD 2026 3 11) TRUE
-- Reported to the Commissioner only: banned on the reading taken, never banned on the readings that need the report to the charity.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner only, on 10 March` EMPTY (YMD 2026 3 13) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` (`the readings taken but with F6.10 read as` `the ban starts on the report to the entity or charity`) TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner only, on 10 March` EMPTY (YMD 2026 3 13) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` (`the readings taken but with F6.10 read as` `the ban starts when both reports have been made`) TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner only, on 10 March` EMPTY (YMD 2026 3 13) TRUE
-- Both reports: the ban starts on the later of the two days (12 March) on the third reading.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` (`the readings taken but with F6.10 read as` `the ban starts when both reports have been made`) TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` EMPTY (YMD 2026 3 11) TRUE
#ASSERT       `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` (`the readings taken but with F6.10 read as` `the ban starts when both reports have been made`) TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` EMPTY (YMD 2026 3 12) TRUE
-- No report, no ban; not a registered charity, no ban.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to nobody` EMPTY (YMD 2026 3 13) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` FALSE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` EMPTY (YMD 2026 3 13) TRUE

-- src:508 | (a) is permitted to do so by the Commissioner under paragraph (9)(d) or (e)(ii), or by the court under Article 20; and
-- src:509 | (b) does so in either case in accordance with any condition on that permission.
-- The exception: permitted (a) AND acting in accordance with any condition (b). A permission given on 1 April 2026.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` (LIST `a permission under Article 19(9)(d) given on 1 April 2026`) (YMD 2026 3 31) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` (LIST `a permission under Article 19(9)(d) given on 1 April 2026`) (YMD 2026 4 1) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` (LIST `a permission under Article 19(9)(d) given on 1 April 2026`) (YMD 2026 4 2) TRUE
-- Permitted but not within the condition on the permission: the exception needs both limbs.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` (LIST `a permission under Article 19(9)(d) given on 1 April 2026`) (YMD 2026 4 2) FALSE
-- A permission by the court counts as one from the Commissioner.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` (LIST `a permission by the court given on 1 April 2026`) (YMD 2026 4 2) TRUE
-- F6.22, the last day of a permission with a time limit ending on 31 May: inside the permission on the reading taken, outside it on the other. 30 May and 1 June are the same on both.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` (LIST `a permission under Article 19(9)(e)(ii) given on 1 April 2026 with a time limit ending on 31 May`) (YMD 2026 5 30) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` (LIST `a permission under Article 19(9)(e)(ii) given on 1 April 2026 with a time limit ending on 31 May`) (YMD 2026 5 31) TRUE
#ASSERT       `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` (LIST `a permission under Article 19(9)(e)(ii) given on 1 April 2026 with a time limit ending on 31 May`) (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE
#ASSERT       `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` (`the readings taken but with F6.22 read as` `the permission ends before the day named`) TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` (LIST `a permission under Article 19(9)(e)(ii) given on 1 April 2026 with a time limit ending on 31 May`) (YMD 2026 5 31) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` (`the readings taken but with F6.22 read as` `the permission ends before the day named`) TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` (LIST `a permission under Article 19(9)(e)(ii) given on 1 April 2026 with a time limit ending on 31 May`) (YMD 2026 5 30) TRUE
-- Withdrawn on 15 May (the notice is withdrawn: the permission lasts until then), and ended by the determination of the issue on 20 May.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` (LIST `a permission under Article 19(9)(d) given on 1 April 2026 and withdrawn on 15 May`) (YMD 2026 5 15) TRUE
#ASSERT       `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` (LIST `a permission under Article 19(9)(d) given on 1 April 2026 and withdrawn on 15 May`) (YMD 2026 5 16) TRUE
#ASSERT       `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` (`the readings taken but with F6.22 read as` `the permission ends before the day named`) TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` (LIST `a permission under Article 19(9)(d) given on 1 April 2026 and withdrawn on 15 May`) (YMD 2026 5 15) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` (LIST `a permission under Article 19(9)(d) given on 1 April 2026 until the issue is determined on 20 May`) (YMD 2026 5 20) TRUE
#ASSERT       `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` (LIST `a permission under Article 19(9)(d) given on 1 April 2026 until the issue is determined on 20 May`) (YMD 2026 5 21) TRUE
-- Several permissions: one in force is enough.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` (LIST `a permission under Article 19(9)(d) given on 1 April 2026 and withdrawn on 15 May`, `a permission by the court given on 1 April 2026`) (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE

-- The prohibition. Acting as a governor while within the ban is the failure; if the person is within the exception, nothing is prohibited.
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 19(10)
#TRACE `Art 19(10) the person must not act as a governor after reporting` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `any person` DOES `act as a governor of a registered charity` `any person` AT 5
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(10) the person must not act as a governor after reporting` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `any person` DOES `act as a governor of a registered charity` `any person` AT 5
-- EXPECT: STANDING act as a governor of a registered charity
#TRACE `Art 19(10) the person must not act as a governor after reporting` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 19(10)
#TRACE `Art 19(10) the standing ban on acting as a governor after reporting` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `any person` DOES `act as a governor of a registered charity` `any person` AT 5

-- src:510 | (11) A person who without reasonable excuse contravenes paragraph (10) commits an offence and is liable to imprisonment for one year and to a fine.
-- (11) A person who without reasonable excuse contravenes paragraph (10) commits an offence and is liable to imprisonment for one year and to a fine.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(11) the person commits an offence` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(11) the person commits an offence` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(11) the person commits an offence` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(11) the person commits an offence` FALSE TRUE
-- The penalty is data: a term of up to 12 months (one year) and a fine for which the Law states no maximum, so none is given.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(11) the penalty for contravening Article 19(10)` EQUALS `Penalty provided` OF (JUST 12), `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`
-- F6.16, the unit of "one year". A term of 366 days from 1 March 2027 ends on 1 March 2028 (2028 has a 29 February): within 12 calendar months, over 365 days.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(11) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of one year` `the readings taken` (YMD 2027 3 1) 366
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(11) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of one year` (`the readings taken but with F6.16 read as` `days`) (YMD 2027 3 1) 366
-- 367 days is over the maximum on both; 365 days is within it on both.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(11) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of one year` `the readings taken` (YMD 2027 3 1) 367
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(11) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of one year` (`the readings taken but with F6.16 read as` `days`) (YMD 2027 3 1) 367
#ASSERT       `Art 19(11) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of one year` `the readings taken` (YMD 2027 3 1) 365
#ASSERT       `Art 19(11) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of one year` (`the readings taken but with F6.16 read as` `days`) (YMD 2027 3 1) 365
-- From 1 March 2026 twelve calendar months end on 1 March 2027, 365 days later: 365 days is within, 366 is not, on both readings.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(11) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of one year` `the readings taken` (YMD 2026 3 1) 365
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(11) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of one year` `the readings taken` (YMD 2026 3 1) 366

-- src:511 | (12) Paragraphs (10) and (11) are not to be construed as requiring an act to be treated as void or invalid merely by virtue of the act constituting a contravention of paragraph (10).
-- (12) Paragraphs (10) and (11) are not to be construed as requiring an act to be treated as void or invalid merely by virtue of the act constituting a contravention of paragraph (10).
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(12) paragraphs (10) and (11) make an act void or invalid merely because it contravened paragraph (10)`

§§ `Trap T9 -- reporting starts the ban, and not reporting is not an offence`

-- (A) A governor with a reportable matter reports at once (to both) and acts the next day, before any permission: contravenes paragraph (10) and, with no excuse, commits the offence.
-- Reports on 10 and 12 March; acts on 13 March.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` EMPTY (YMD 2026 3 13) TRUE
#ASSERT       `Art 19(11) the person commits an offence` (`Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to the Commissioner on 10 March and to the charity on 12 March` EMPTY (YMD 2026 3 13) TRUE) FALSE
-- (B) The same governor does not report and acts: in breach of paragraph (2) (the time for a prompt report has run out), barred by paragraph (8) -- and no offence under (11), because paragraph (8) is not mentioned there.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(2) the governor is in breach of paragraph (2)` `the readings taken` `the number of days not given` (YMD 2026 3 13) `Gus with a reportable matter` `position of Gus: reported to nobody`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to nobody` EMPTY (YMD 2026 3 13) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(11) the person commits an offence` (`Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to nobody` EMPTY (YMD 2026 3 13) TRUE) FALSE
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 19(8)
#TRACE `Art 19(8) the person must not act as a governor while in breach of Article 19(2) or (4)` TRUE (`Art 19(2) the governor is in breach of paragraph (2)` `the readings taken` `the number of days not given` (YMD 2026 3 13) `Gus with a reportable matter` `position of Gus: reported to nobody`) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `any person` DOES `act as a governor of a registered charity` `any person` AT 5
-- (C) A governor with no reportable matter who ignores the request for a declaration under paragraph (4): barred by paragraph (8), and outside paragraph (10) altogether (nothing was reported).
#ASSERT       `Art 19(4) the governor is in breach of paragraph (4)` `the readings taken` TRUE (YMD 2026 6 9) `Gwen with no reportable matter` `Gwen: notified on 1 June 2026, no declaration yet`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the readings taken` TRUE `position of Gus: reported to nobody` EMPTY (YMD 2026 6 9) TRUE
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 19(8)
#TRACE `Art 19(8) the person must not act as a governor while in breach of Article 19(2) or (4)` TRUE FALSE (`Art 19(4) the governor is in breach of paragraph (4)` `the readings taken` TRUE (YMD 2026 6 9) `Gwen with no reportable matter` `Gwen: notified on 1 June 2026, no declaration yet`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `any person` DOES `act as a governor of a registered charity` `any person` AT 5

-- src:512 | (13) If at any time the Commissioner suspects that a governor of a registered charity may have breached paragraph (2), the Commissioner may, without prejudice to any other of his or her powers, apply to the court to determine whether the governor is a fit and proper person to be a governor.
-- (13) If at any time the Commissioner suspects that a governor of a registered charity may have breached paragraph (2), the Commissioner may apply to the court to determine whether the governor is a fit and proper person.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(13) the Commissioner may apply to the court` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `apply to the court to determine whether the governor is a fit and proper person` `the Commissioner` AT 3
-- EXPECT: STANDING apply to the court to determine whether the governor is a fit and proper person
#TRACE `Art 19(13) the Commissioner may apply to the court` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- Without the suspicion, or for an entity that is not a registered charity, there is no such power.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(13) the Commissioner may apply to the court` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 19(13) the Commissioner may apply to the court` FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

§§ `Edges added after the mutation sweep found them untested`

-- F6.9: a disqualification imposed on the very day it is asked about. It has been imposed on that day (reading taken), and it is in force on that day (the other reading); the day before, neither.
`a disqualification elsewhere imposed on 15 June 2026` MEANS `Disqualification elsewhere` OF (YMD 2026 6 15), NOTHING
`Quin disqualified as a charity trustee on 15 June 2026` MEANS `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` OF (`Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Quin", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, (LIST `a disqualification elsewhere imposed on 15 June 2026`), EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE
-- src:486 | (c) has been disqualified from or for being a charity trustee or trustee for a charity under the law of any part of the United Kingdom, or from holding any equivalent position under the law of any other jurisdiction;
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1)(c) the person has been disqualified as a charity trustee or from an equivalent position` `the readings taken` (YMD 2026 6 15) `Quin disqualified as a charity trustee on 15 June 2026`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(1)(c) the person has been disqualified as a charity trustee or from an equivalent position` `the readings taken` (YMD 2026 6 14) `Quin disqualified as a charity trustee on 15 June 2026`
#ASSERT       `Art 19(1)(c) the person has been disqualified as a charity trustee or from an equivalent position` (`the readings taken but with F6.9 read as` `only a disqualification still in force counts`) (YMD 2026 6 15) `Quin disqualified as a charity trustee on 15 June 2026`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(1)(c) the person has been disqualified as a charity trustee or from an equivalent position` (`the readings taken but with F6.9 read as` `only a disqualification still in force counts`) (YMD 2026 6 14) `Quin disqualified as a charity trustee on 15 June 2026`

-- F6.12, reading C: the matter arose on 1 March, the governor became aware on 20 March; ten days count as prompt. A report on 30 March is ten days after awareness: prompt; on 31 March, eleven: not.
`position of Gus: arose on 1 March 2026, aware on 20 March, reported to both on 30 March` MEANS `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 3 20), JUST (YMD 2026 3 30), JUST (YMD 2026 3 30), FALSE, FALSE
`position of Gus: arose on 1 March 2026, aware on 20 March, unreported` MEANS `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 3 20), NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, TRUE
-- src:492 | (2) A governor of an entity applying for registration, or of a registered charity, must report any reportable matter promptly to that entity or charity and to the Commissioner.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(2) the report made on the date is prompt` (`the readings taken but with F6.12 read as` `promptness is a number of days from the governor becoming aware of the matter`) `ten days` `position of Gus: arose on 1 March 2026, aware on 20 March, reported to both on 30 March` (YMD 2026 3 30)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(2) the report made on the date is prompt` (`the readings taken but with F6.12 read as` `promptness is a number of days from the governor becoming aware of the matter`) `ten days` `position of Gus: arose on 1 March 2026, aware on 20 March, reported to both on 30 March` (YMD 2026 3 31)
-- ... and the breach: the last prompt day is 30 March; the governor is in breach from 31 March.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(2) the governor is in breach of paragraph (2)` (`the readings taken but with F6.12 read as` `promptness is a number of days from the governor becoming aware of the matter`) `ten days` (YMD 2026 3 30) `Gus with a reportable matter` `position of Gus: arose on 1 March 2026, aware on 20 March, unreported`
#ASSERT       `Art 19(2) the governor is in breach of paragraph (2)` (`the readings taken but with F6.12 read as` `promptness is a number of days from the governor becoming aware of the matter`) `ten days` (YMD 2026 3 31) `Gus with a reportable matter` `position of Gus: arose on 1 March 2026, aware on 20 March, unreported`
-- On the counting from the matter arising, the awareness is irrelevant: 31 March is long past the last prompt day, 11 March.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(2) the governor is in breach of paragraph (2)` (`the readings taken but with F6.12 read as` `promptness is a number of days from the matter arising`) `ten days` (YMD 2026 3 30) `Gus with a reportable matter` `position of Gus: arose on 1 March 2026, aware on 20 March, unreported`

-- F6.20, the other reading with no declaration at all: not in time.
-- src:493 | (3) A governor of an entity applying for registration must, if there is no reportable matter in relation to that governor, provide to the entity a declaration to that effect before the application is made.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(3) the declaration was provided before the application was made` (`the readings taken but with F6.20 read as` `a declaration must be given on an earlier day than the application`) NOTHING (YMD 2026 5 10)

-- F6.21, the other reading: the notification counts from the day it is given. On the day of the notification, once a reasonable time is said to have passed, in breach; the day before it, not yet notified.
-- src:494 | (4) A governor of a registered charity must, if there is no reportable matter in relation to that governor, provide to the charity a declaration to that effect when notified by the charity that it is preparing its annual return.
#ASSERT       `Art 19(4) the governor is in breach of paragraph (4)` (`the readings taken but with F6.21 read as` `the governor is in breach once a reasonable time has passed after the notification`) TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) `Gwen with no reportable matter` `Gwen: notified on 1 June 2026, no declaration yet, a reasonable time has passed`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 19(4) the governor is in breach of paragraph (4)` (`the readings taken but with F6.21 read as` `the governor is in breach once a reasonable time has passed after the notification`) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 31) `Gwen with no reportable matter` `Gwen: notified on 1 June 2026, no declaration yet, a reasonable time has passed`
